  "verbalization": "Albinoside Ii appears to act through a shared mechanism involving Peptide deformylase, which is the target of multiple compounds—Sugiol, Cinnabaramide C, and 2-(alpha-D-galactosyl)glycerol. All three of these compounds are predicted to interact with UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4, suggesting a potential pathway where Albinoside Ii may exert its effects via a similar mechanism. The evidence indicates that Albinoside Ii may target Peptide deformylase, which in turn influences UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4, possibly through a common intermediate. This suggests a possible functional link between Albinoside Ii and UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4, where the drug's activity is mediated by a shared target or a downstream effect on the enzyme. The integration of these paths highlights a potential role for Peptide deformylase as a critical node in the pathway, with Albinoside Ii possibly acting through a similar mechanism as the other compounds.",
